  data: {
    LLM: "In 1-card rounds, an Ace is a guaranteed trick. In higher rounds, bid conservatively—it is usually easier to win an extra trick than to lose one you didn't want.\n\nCounting the Total: Pay attention to the sum of the bids. If the total is much higher than the tricks available, play defensively as players will be fighting over every trick.\n\nThe Dealer's Trap: As the dealer, use your forced-bid constraint to create a 'low-bid' round if you have a weak hand, forcing others to fight for high tricks while you safely duck with your low cards.",
    Player: "In 1-card rounds, an Ace is a guaranteed trick. In higher rounds, bid conservatively—it is usually easier to win an extra trick than to lose one you didn't want.\n\nCounting the Total: Pay attention to the sum of the bids. If the total is much higher than the tricks available, play defensively as players will be fighting over every trick.\n\nThe Dealer's Trap: As the dealer, use your forced-bid constraint to create a 'low-bid' round if you have a weak hand, forcing others to fight for high tricks while you safely duck with your low cards.",
